desc:TwoStorms Multiband
tags: dynamics compressor multiband expander
author: TwoStorms
version: 1.0

// A multiband compressor / expander with an Act built in: its output gain, meters, Auto (Target, Match, Reference),
// Drive link and Finale are a TwoStorms Act, so TwoStorms Gain Stage lists and stages it like one.
// One to four bands: a tick box in front of each of three crossover frequencies (sorted, whichever box holds which).
// Zero-latency Linkwitz-Riley crossovers (24 dB/oct, the bands stay in phase and add back flat), or linear phase
// (the bands add back to exactly the input; adds latency). Per band: On, Solo, Compress or Expand (a conventional
// expander), threshold, ratio, knee, attack, release, range (negative cuts, positive lifts) and makeup. For every band:
// peak, RMS or hybrid detection, Mono, Stereo, Mid/Side or Left/Right with stereo link (Max or power average), detector
// from the main input or a sidechain (inputs 3-4, split by the same crossovers), input, dry/wet, Delta, optional lookahead.
// Per band also hold, makeup by hand or auto, and a Character (Clean VCA, Opto, FET, Vari-mu, or Custom: envelope,
// release mode, curve, feedback, saturation).
// "Set thresholds" listens and sets every band's threshold so it reaches its range on the loudest moments.
// A/B sets with hold-to-hear level-matched Bypass and Swap. Needs REAPER 6.74 or newer.

slider1:0<0,3,1{2,4,6,8}>-Channels
slider2:0<0,2,1{Auto,Always,Never}>-Finale (Auto = the last Act in the chain)
slider3:0<0,2,1{Peak,RMS,LUFS}>-Auto measure
slider4:-12<-60,0,0.01>-Auto target
slider5:4<0,7,1{Manual,1 s,2 s,3 s,5 s,10 s,20 s,30 s}>-Auto time
slider6:1<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Link 1-2
slider7:1<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Link 3-4
slider8:1<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Link 5-6
slider9:1<0,1,1{Off,On}>-Link 7-8
slider10:0<-100,60,0.01>-Ch1 gain (dB, -100 = -inf)
